# Software Engineer Portfolio - Frontend

A modern, fully responsive, and internationalized portfolio website for a software engineer and web developer. Built with Vue 3, TypeScript, and TailwindCSS, designed to integrate seamlessly with a Laravel API backend.

## ✨ Features

- **Vue 3 Composition API**: Modern, reactive, and maintainable codebase using `<script setup>`.
- **TypeScript**: Strict typing for robust development.
- **TailwindCSS**: Utility-first CSS framework for rapid, responsive UI development with a custom naval/navy theme.
- **Internationalization (i18n)**: Full support for English (EN), Arabic (AR), and Turkish (TR) with automatic RTL/LTR layout switching.
- **State Management**: Pinia stores for global state and API data caching.
- **Routing**: Vue Router 5 for seamless Single Page Application (SPA) navigation.
- **API Ready**: Pre-configured Axios wrapper with interceptors ready to consume Laravel APIs.
- **Modern UI Components**: Built with Headless UI, VueUse, and Iconify for accessible and highly customizable elements.
- **Responsive Design**: Mobile-first approach ensuring perfect display on all devices.

## 🛠️ Tech Stack

- **Framework**: Vue 3.x
- **Build Tool**: Vite
- **Language**: TypeScript
- **Styling**: TailwindCSS 3.4.x
- **Routing**: Vue Router 5.x
- **State Management**: Pinia
- **HTTP Client**: Axios 1.20.x
- **i18n**: Vue I18n 11.x
- **UI/Icons**: Headless UI, VueUse, Iconify

## 📦 Prerequisites

Before you begin, ensure you have the following installed on your machine:
- [Node.js](https://nodejs.org/) (v18.x or higher recommended)
- [npm](https://www.npmjs.com/) (comes with Node.js)

## 🚀 Installation & Setup

1. **Clone the repository**
   ```bash
   git clone https://github.com/your-username/your-portfolio-frontend.git
   cd your-portfolio-frontend
   ```

2. **Install dependencies**
   ```bash
   npm install
   ```

3. **Set up environment variables**
   Create a `.env` file in the root directory and add your backend API URL:
   ```env
   VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:8000/api
   ```

4. **Run the development server**
   ```bash
   npm run dev
   ```
   The application will be available at `http://localhost:5173`.

## 📜 Available Scripts

- `npm run dev`: Starts the Vite development server with hot-module replacement (HMR).
- `npm run build`: Compiles and minifies for production to the `dist` folder.
- `npm run preview`: Previews the production build locally.
- `npm run type-check`: Runs TypeScript type checking without emitting files.

## 📁 Project Structure

```text
src/
├── assets/         # Static assets (images, fonts)
├── components/     # Reusable UI and layout components
│   ├── layout/     # Navbar, Footer
│   └── ui/         # Buttons, Cards, Language Switcher, etc.
├── composables/    # Custom Vue hooks (e.g., useApi)
├── layouts/        # Main layout wrapper (DefaultLayout.vue)
├── locales/        # i18n translation files (en.json, ar.json, tr.json)
├── router/         # Vue Router configuration
├── stores/         # Pinia state management stores
├── types/          # TypeScript interfaces and types
├── views/          # Page-level components (Home, Projects, Contact)
├── App.vue         # Root component
├── main.ts         # App entry point
└── style.css       # Global TailwindCSS styles
```

## 🌍 Internationalization (i18n)

The app supports English, Arabic, and Turkish. 
- Translations are stored in `src/locales/*.json`.
- The app automatically handles RTL (Right-to-Left) layout switching when Arabic is selected.
- The backend API is expected to return localized data based on the `Accept-Language` header sent by the frontend.

## 🔌 Backend Integration

This frontend is designed to work independently from a Laravel API. 
- API calls are managed via a centralized Axios instance found in `src/composables/useApi.ts`.
- Base URL and timeout configurations are handled via environment variables.
- Expected data formats from the backend are defined in `src/types/`.

